cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "rk-recall: Drift Convergence Theorem for Runge-Kutta via ω-Limit-Set Projection"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "rk-recall Contributors"
    email: "17319939601@163.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jinggu-glitch/rk-recall"
url: "https://github.com/jinggu-glitch/rk-recall"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained numerical-integration module that tames Runge-Kutta error
  accumulation via ω-limit-set projection (§3.26.16 Drift Convergence
  Theorem) and Pyragas→Γ phase locking (§3.26.17). The core theorem proves
  drift ε_leaf(T_baseline) → 0 as T_baseline → ∞ (Birkhoff ergodic +
  Poincaré recurrence), a property not possessed by Symplectic integrators,
  Projected RK, or Pyragas DFC. The algorithm is fully decoupled from any
  specific ODE and uses NO external oracle: the correction anchor (hope_p)
  is located in closed form from the trajectory's own ω-limit set, in pure
  numpy. Verified on harmonic oscillator (analytical available), Lorenz
  (chaotic, no analytical), and Van der Pol (nonlinear, no closed-form).
  Honest limitations: drift → 0 is asymptotic (not strict 0, bounded by
  floating-point precision); phase → O(h²) (not strict 0, bounded by RK4
  local error); requires bounded systems (ω-limit set must exist); not
  suitable for stiff or high-dimensional (d > 3) systems.
keywords:
  - numerical-integration
  - runge-kutta
  - drift-convergence
  - ergodic-theorem
  - limit-cycle
  - omega-limit-set
  - pyragas-dfc
  - phase-locking
  - dynamical-systems
  - no-oracle
